    <p class="eyebrow mt-2" style="color:#0057B7">Since 2014</p>
    <h2 class="h-sec mt-3 mb-5">A campaign of destruction, not a single invasion</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">Russia's war against Ukraine did not start in February 2022. It began in February–March 2014, when Russian soldiers without insignia seized Crimea's parliament and military bases in the aftermath of Ukraine's Revolution of Dignity, staged a referendum the international community rejected as illegal, and annexed the peninsula. Weeks later, Russian-backed forces seized territory across Ukraine's Donbas region. The UN human rights office estimates 14,200–14,400 people were killed in that conflict between April 2014 and the end of 2021 — before the full-scale invasion even began — and hundreds of thousands more were displaced from their homes.</p>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-sm">
      <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Russian_annexation_of_Crimea" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">Timeline of the annexation</a>
      <a href="https://ukraine.un.org/sites/default/files/2022-02/Conflict-related%20civilian%20casualties%20as%20of%2031%20December%202021%20(rev%2027%20January%202022)%20corr%20EN_0.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">UN OHCHR casualty report</a>
    </div>

    <p class="eyebrow mt-16" style="color:#0057B7">How the world names this</p>
    <h2 class="h-sec mt-3 mb-5">Genocide and terror</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">Under the 1948 Genocide Convention, genocide means acts like killing, causing serious harm, deliberately inflicting conditions aimed at a group's destruction, or forcibly transferring children — committed with intent to destroy a national group in whole or in part. In May 2022, the New Lines Institute for Strategy and Policy and the Raoul Wallenberg Centre for Human Rights, backed by 35 international genocide and atrocity-crime experts, published a legal analysis finding reasonable grounds that Russia has directly and publicly incited genocide against the Ukrainian people, and identified a serious risk of genocide under the Convention. On 27 April, the Parliamentary Assembly of the Council of Europe went further and formally recognised the forced deportation of Ukrainian children to Russia as genocide, by a vote of 87 to 1.</p>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-sm">
      <a href="https://newlinesinstitute.org/rules-based-international-order/genocide/the-russian-federations-escalating-commission-of-genocide-in-ukraine-a-legal-analysis/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">New Lines Institute legal analysis</a>
      <a href="https://www.ukrainianworldcongress.org/pace-recognizes-deportations-of-ukrainian-children-genocide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">PACE resolution coverage</a>
    </div>

    <p class="eyebrow mt-16" style="color:#0057B7">A state that uses terror</p>
    <h2 class="h-sec mt-3 mb-5">Recognised as a state sponsor of terrorism</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">On 23 November 2022, the European Parliament adopted a resolution recognising the Russian Federation as a state sponsor of terrorism and a state that uses terrorist methods, by 494 votes to 58 with 44 abstentions, in response to deliberate attacks on civilians and the systematic destruction of civilian infrastructure. The resolution states these atrocities constitute war crimes and acts of terror against the Ukrainian people. Lithuania, Latvia, Estonia and Poland have each gone further and formally designated Russia a state sponsor of terrorism in their own national parliaments. We stand firmly behind this position — not as a slogan, but as a sober description of what our friends and communities have lived through.</p>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-sm">
      <a href="https://www.europarl.europa.eu/news/en/press-room/20221118IPR55707/european-parliament-declares-russia-to-be-a-state-sponsor-of-terrorism" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">European Parliament announcement</a>
      <a href="https://kyivindependent.com/ukraine-war-latest-russia-bombards-ukraines-infrastructure-after-european-parliament-declares-it-state-sponsor-of-terrorism/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold underline underline-offset-2">The Kyiv Independent</a>
    </div>

    <p class="eyebrow mt-16" style="color:#0057B7">Our home region</p>
    <h2 class="h-sec mt-3 mb-5">What this means in Chernihiv Oblast</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed">Chernihiv Oblast, where Elysium+ was founded, was among the first regions attacked and besieged in the opening weeks of the full-scale invasion. Russian forces encircled Chernihiv city, cut off evacuation routes, and bombed residential areas. A bombing on 3 March 2022 killed 47 people — Amnesty International and Human Rights Watch both described the strike as a likely war crime. On 16 March, a Russian attack on civilians queuing for bread killed at least 18 more. On 23 March, the last road bridge out of the city was destroyed, cutting off the evacuation of the wounded and the delivery of humanitarian aid.</p>

