      <div class="card p-6">
        <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold">Yahidne: 28 days in a school basement</p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">On 3 March 2022, Russian soldiers occupying the village of Yahidne, Chernihiv Oblast, forced 368 residents — including 80 children, the youngest six weeks old — into the local school's basement, giving each person roughly 50cm of space, for 28 days without adequate food, medical care or ventilation. Ten people died underground; Ukrainian prosecutors have since charged Russian soldiers over those deaths. Stories like this are not distant headlines to us — they are the reality of the communities we work with.</p>
