        <p class="font-display text-lg font-bold">Documented across the oblast — and still happening</p>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">The UN Human Rights Monitoring Mission in Ukraine (OHCHR) has verified unlawful killings, including summary executions, of civilians in more than 30 settlements across Chernihiv Oblast under Russian military control in 2022 — part of a wider pattern documented across more than 100 towns and villages in the Kyiv, Chernihiv and Sumy regions. It has not stopped: drone and missile strikes on homes, schools and civilian infrastructure across the oblast continue today.</p>
